// The ONE deploy that cannot be done from the dashboard.
//
// A Durable Object namespace is created by a migration at upload time, and
// the dashboard has no button for it (its binding picker only lists
// namespaces that already exist). So the first deploy of `SaveRoom` goes
// through wrangler, once, from the repo root:
//
//     npx wrangler login
//     npx wrangler deploy --config server/wrangler.jsonc
//
// Nothing is installed into the repo — `npx` fetches wrangler into its own
// cache — and the page keeps its rule of no npm and no build step; this is
// the server, which was always the one piece that is not a file GitHub
// Pages serves. After this deploy the code can go on being pasted into the
// dashboard editor as before: the namespace and the binding stay.
//
// `name` must be the worker that already exists, so the URL in
// `src/ui/sync.js` keeps pointing at the same place. A KV binding that the
// dashboard had on it is dropped by this deploy, which is intended.
{
  "name": "rogulidle-save",
  "main": "save-worker.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-01",
  "durable_objects": {
    "bindings": [
      { "name": "SAVES", "class_name": "SaveRoom" }
    ]
  },
  "migrations": [
    { "tag": "v1", "new_sqlite_classes": ["SaveRoom"] }
  ]
}
